      KeyError: 'does-not-exist'
+
+  A valueless option cannot start a multiline value.  If an indented
+  continuation line follows such an option, the parser raises
+  :exc:`MultilineContinuationError`, a subclass of :exc:`ParsingError`,
+  exposing the parsing source, the one-based line number of the offending
+  continuation line and the exact offending line.  Indented continuation
+  lines after an option that already has a value on its option line remain
+  valid multiline values.
 
 * *delimiters*, default value: ``('=', ':')``
 
@@ -1372,6 +1380,17 @@
    headers.
 
 
+.. exception:: MultilineContinuationError
+
+   Exception raised when a valueless option is followed by an indented
+   continuation line.  Subclass of :exc:`ParsingError`.
+
+   The constructor stores the parsing source in ``source``, the one-based
+   line number in ``lineno`` and the exact offending line in ``line``; its
+   ``args`` are ``(source, lineno, line)``.  As with :exc:`ParsingError`,
+   the offending entry is also recorded in ``errors``.
+
+
 .. exception:: ParsingError
 
    Exception raised when errors occur attempting to parse a file.
